{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gs carries the ownership step in serving, at head 1ccad3e20fb93a697e2d934f53a9e1eb7f2d8947 on request/multi-resident-coordination, rebased onto main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 57adc242cec02a41eaf74eeacc98f4cd5506220b. Both files in this package are byte-identical to that candidate; #6349 touched nothing here. The serve seam was re-read at this head regardless, and the order still holds: bind, claim, close-the-listener-on-refusal, deferred close-then-release, advertise, serve.\n\nserveCommand binds, claims, and only then serves. Binding stays first so the claim carries the address actually served including a port the kernel chose, but binding no longer authorizes anything: a start that does not win the claim closes its listener and returns the refusal without answering a single request, and the advertisement is written only after ownership is held. On shutdown the listener is closed before the claim is released, under a fresh ten-second context, so whoever wins the freed claim cannot find this process still answering. claimResidency wires the resident client's probe in with a two-second deadline; the command is where the two packages meet.\n\nTests at this head, in cmd/gs/main_test.go: a second in-process serve on a held repository returns a ResidentHeldError naming the incumbent's URL, leaves the claim byte-identical and the advertisement untouched, and the repository can be served again once the first stops; a claim left by a dead owner, pointing at a closed port, is recovered rather than wedging the repository; and at the executable level a second real gs serve process exits non-zero with the incumbent's address in its output, leaves claim and advertisement alone, and the incumbent keeps answering, after which interrupting it releases the claim and an ordinary start serves.\n\nOne executable-level test asserted the previous contract — that a second service took the advertisement over, and that stopping the replaced one left the successor advertised. That scenario is now unreachable, so it is replaced by the refusal it became rather than deleted silently; the withdrawal guard it protected is covered on the claim in internal/app.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 34c5f09e2f5bc4e4fa5acb7404ae9b7df4808e52 at f22fa1dd, for my merge to retire later. It is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in codex's report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"1ccad3e20fb93a697e2d934f53a9e1eb7f2d8947","path":"cmd/gs"}}